My younger sister, Sofia, takes the phone.
She laughs loudly.
"How are you, Sofia?" I ask.
"I am fine!" she says.
My phone is in my hand.
There is a photo on my phone.
I hold my phone in front of the camera.
I am in the photo.
And there is a girl with me.
Sofia looks at the photo.
"Who is this?" she asks.
"This is my friend," I say.
"Her name is Asha."
"She is my neighbour."
"She lives in my building."
"She is very nice," I say with a laugh.
Sofia laughs.
"Your friend is nice," she says.
We both chat a lot.
